Build a standalone C++ load client using the actual dialer, TLS, WebSocketSock, P2P-v2 serializer/decoder and buffered-receive readiness. Python only orchestrates real nodes, stopped-fixture clones, RPC, per-thread CPU samples and machine-readable receipts; peers stay in C++ and never request compact blocks.

Preserve the measured legacy corpus separately and add native J3 MiniWallet/miner generation for forty real approximately8/32MB blocks plus a validated relay candidate. Guard shared-host RSS and swap, record skipped250/500-peer cells explicitly, and capture actual wire/cache counters. Native corpus consensus execution remains pending corrected-core gates.

Original-Source: N2a e4e5ec0220098b630935c6f85779e4e01f3282de load-client/runner owners and fixups plus65e5ac7c7f native generator/receipts folded. Existing p2p-load target is absent from corrected base, so include it with the corpus owner.

